<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of Aden</h1><p class="st-meta">1937 CE – 1963 CE · capital Aden</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Aden as a British Crown colony, a booming port and military base whose politics fed the nationalist movement in South Arabia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/government-of-india">Government of India</a> Act of 1935, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aden-settlement">Aden Settlement</a> was separated from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/british-raj">British India</a> and became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-colony">Crown colony</a> on 1 April 1937, governed directly from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> by a governor. It covered the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a>, Crater, Steamer Point and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/little-aden">Little Aden</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> was one of the world's busiest ports, serving ships on the Suez route. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bp">British Petroleum</a> refinery opened at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/little-aden">Little Aden</a> in 1954, and from 1960 Aden housed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a> Command. The population of Yemenis, Indians, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somalis</a> and a dwindling Jewish community grew rapidly, and strong trade unions, led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden-trades-union-congress">Aden Trades Union Congress</a>, became the base of anti-colonial politics.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In January 1963, against nationalist opposition, the colony joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federation-of-south-arabia">Federation of South Arabia</a> and became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-aden">State of Aden</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/colony-of-aden.jpg" alt="Colony of Aden" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: O · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Aden_(1937%E2%80%931963).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1937 CE – 1963 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Aden</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bernard Reilly, Charles Johnston</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam, with Hindu, Jewish and Christian minorities</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/yemen">Yemen</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Aden Colony</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1950&amp;focus=colony-of-aden" aria-label="Colony of Aden on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5916 1701 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Colony of Aden lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6236 1957L6236 1957M6236 1957L4997 651M6236 1957L6236 1957"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6236 1957h0M4997 651h0M6236 1957h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6236 1957h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6236 1957h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Aden. <a href="/atlas?year=1950&amp;focus=colony-of-aden">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
